<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-limbform-audit-lobo-limbform-morphology-code-traceability> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — Code-to-model traceability: 75/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The module docstring states the formalism table by table and names the paper section it follows; the radius rule, the sub-joint rule, the Fig. 1 colour conventions and the bones-for-tetrapods-only convention are documented where they are implemented. As with the Planform sibling, the papers give no numbered equations, so the rules were confirmed against the database rather than quoted. Evidence: 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L1–L13: what is reproduced and from which figure <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L1-L13>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L113–L125: colour and bone conventions named <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L113-L125>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L330–L352: control_points(): rule and padding stated <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L330-L352>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology-code-traceability> ;
    pk:hasProbability 7.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-limbform-audit-lobo-limbform-morphology-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — Model fidelity to source: 85/100" ;
    dct:references <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/lobo-limbform-morphology-1> ;
    rdfs:comment "The encoding is read as the formalism defines it: Link rows are segments with Type, Dist, Ang, Side/Reversed/Inverted and NumBones; JointParam radii are one per bisector of consecutive segments at the joint or +90/+180/+270 deg for a terminal joint; LinkSubJoint places grafts at (Dist, Ang) on their host segment; Digit rows hang off the hand/foot segment. The rule is checked against every joint at load time (3137/3146) and the 9 under-parameterised joints are padded with the joint's mean radius, which is stated in the code. Short of full marks because the papers describe the formalism in prose, so the bisector-order convention and the 'host segment counts twice' rule for sub-joints were established by checking the database, and because the residual silhouette differences against Fig. 1 (below) leave the Ang convention not fully confirmed. Evidence: 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L26–L47: the formalism as implemented <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L26-L47>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L222–L260: load_morphologies(): the five tables read <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L222-L260>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L314–L352: _edges_of()/control_points(): the radius rule, edge order kept <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L314-L352>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L606–L620: check_encoding(): the rule checked on every joint <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L606-L620>." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:hasProbability 8.5e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/2026-10-14-limbform-audit-lobo-limbform-morphology-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "LimbformDB limb morphologies — Morphometric validation: 55/100" ;
    rdfs:comment "The script computes per-morphology morphometrics (segment and digit counts, proximodistal path length, bounding box, silhouette area) and writes them as CSV, and the measurements sidecar compares the five Fig. 1 wild types quantitatively with the paper's own figure (segment and digit counts against the labelled graphs A'-E', all equal; silhouette IoU and bounding-box aspect against the cartoons A''-E''). Those are comparisons with the source authors' rendering of the same data, not with measurements of real limbs, and the IoU values themselves show the agreement is partial. Evidence: 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L587–L604: morphometrics() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L587-L604>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L569–L585: longest_path_length(): proximodistal length <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L569-L585>; 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py L869–L883: write_csv() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/747c57f/2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py#L869-L883>; limbform_wildtype_gallery.png (generated output, not in repo): the output measured against Fig. 1 (see the measurements sidecar) — limbform_wildtype_gallery.png: rendered output of 2014-lobo-limbform-morphology.py at 747c57f, image/png, 620043 B, 2400×1875 px, sha256 d561f4aab10756976c3fd5caf7a8c516da13c1cd9395d6cb5a54b8a2f5b10236. Measurements (measure_outputs.py): morphologies decoded = 555 count (reference 565, rows in LimbformDB 2.1.0 Morphology table) [Morphology rows with at least one Link (segment) row] — the rest are outcome labels without geometry (Lethal, No limb, ...); joints obeying the radius rule = 3137 count (reference 3146, all joints; the rule is the formalism's (Regeneration 1:37, Fig. 2)) [joints whose JointParam count equals the number of incident segments (3 for a terminal joint; a sub-joint counts its host segment twice)]; segments, #1 Wild type, right forelimb = 3 count (reference 3, Lobo et al. 2014 Regeneration Fig. 1 A′: Upper arm, Fore arm, Hand; digits 1-4) [Link rows of the morphology]; digits, #1 Wild type, right forelimb = 4 count (reference 4, Lobo et al. 2014 Regeneration Fig. 1 A′: Upper arm, Fore arm, Hand; digits 1-4) [Digit rows of the morphology]; segments, #280 Wild type, right hindlimb = 3 count (reference 3, Lobo et al. 2014 Regeneration Fig. 1 B′: Thigh, Shank, Foot; digits 1-5 plus the prehallux node) [Link rows of the morphology]; digits, #280 Wild type, right hindlimb = 6 count (reference 6, Lobo et al. 2014 Regeneration Fig. 1 B′: Thigh, Shank, Foot; digits 1-5 plus the prehallux node) [Digit rows of the morphology]; segments, #314 Wild type, right walking leg, fiddler crab = 7 count (reference 7, Lobo et al. 2014 Regeneration Fig. 1 C′: Coxa, Basis, Ischium, Merus, Carpus, Propus, Dactyl) [Link rows of the morphology]; segments, #490 Wild type, right metathoracic (T3) leg, cricket nymph = 8 count (reference 8, Lobo et al. 2014 Regeneration Fig. 1 D′: Coxa, Trochanter, Femur, Tibia, Tarsus 1-4 (as labelled)) [Link rows of the morphology]; segments, #491 Wild type, right leg I, huntsman spider = 7 count (reference 7, Lobo et al. 2014 Regeneration Fig. 1 E′: Coxa, Trochanter, Femur, Patella, Tibia, Metatarsus, Tarsus) [Link rows of the morphology]; silhouette IoU vs Fig. 1 A'', #1 Wild type, right forelimb = 0.6448 ratio (reference 1.0, the paper's own rendering of the same database entry) [largest ink component of the cartoon panel (holes filled) and the decoded silhouette, each cropped to its bounding box and scaled to a 200-px canvas (aspect kept); intersection over union, best of 8 rotations/reflections (rot180+mirror)] — bones, digits and gradient are inside the outline, so this compares outer shape only; the cartoon is a 560-px JPEG, which bounds the achievable IoU below 1; bounding-box aspect, #1 Wild type, right forelimb = 1.5738 ratio (reference 1.463, same statistic on the Fig. 1 A'' cartoon) [longer / shorter side of the decoded silhouette's bounding box]; silhouette IoU vs Fig. 1 B'', #280 Wild type, right hindlimb = 0.4105 ratio (reference 1.0, the paper's own rendering of the same database entry) [largest ink component of the cartoon panel (holes filled) and the decoded silhouette, each cropped to its bounding box and scaled to a 200-px canvas (aspect kept); intersection over union, best of 8 rotations/reflections (rot0+mirror)] — bones, digits and gradient are inside the outline, so this compares outer shape only; the cartoon is a 560-px JPEG, which bounds the achievable IoU below 1; bounding-box aspect, #280 Wild type, right hindlimb = 1.4696 ratio (reference 1.832, same statistic on the Fig. 1 B'' cartoon) [longer / shorter side of the decoded silhouette's bounding box]; silhouette IoU vs Fig. 1 C'', #314 Wild type, right walking leg, fiddler crab = 0.4313 ratio (reference 1.0, the paper's own rendering of the same database entry) [largest ink component of the cartoon panel (holes filled) and the decoded silhouette, each cropped to its bounding box and scaled to a 200-px canvas (aspect kept); intersection over union, best of 8 rotations/reflections (rot180+mirror)] — bones, digits and gradient are inside the outline, so this compares outer shape only; the cartoon is a 560-px JPEG, which bounds the achievable IoU below 1; bounding-box aspect, #314 Wild type, right walking leg, fiddler crab = 1.2414 ratio (reference 1.051, same statistic on the Fig. 1 C'' cartoon) [longer / shorter side of the decoded silhouette's bounding box]; silhouette IoU vs Fig. 1 D'', #490 Wild type, right metathoracic (T3) leg, cricket nymph = 0.7432 ratio (reference 1.0, the paper's own rendering of the same database entry) [largest ink component of the cartoon panel (holes filled) and the decoded silhouette, each cropped to its bounding box and scaled to a 200-px canvas (aspect kept); intersection over union, best of 8 rotations/reflections (rot180+mirror)] — bones, digits and gradient are inside the outline, so this compares outer shape only; the cartoon is a 560-px JPEG, which bounds the achievable IoU below 1; bounding-box aspect, #490 Wild type, right metathoracic (T3) leg, cricket nymph = 1.1346 ratio (reference 1.084, same statistic on the Fig. 1 D'' cartoon) [longer / shorter side of the decoded silhouette's bounding box]; silhouette IoU vs Fig. 1 E'', #491 Wild type, right leg I, huntsman spider = 0.4851 ratio (reference 1.0, the paper's own rendering of the same database entry) [largest ink component of the cartoon panel (holes filled) and the decoded silhouette, each cropped to its bounding box and scaled to a 200-px canvas (aspect kept); intersection over union, best of 8 rotations/reflections (rot180+mirror)] — bones, digits and gradient are inside the outline, so this compares outer shape only; the cartoon is a 560-px JPEG, which bounds the achievable IoU below 1; bounding-box aspect, #491 Wild type, right leg I, huntsman spider = 1.5391 ratio (reference 1.455, same statistic on the Fig. 1 E'' cartoon) [longer / shorter side of the decoded silhouette's bounding box]." ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/claude-fable-5-1> ;
    pk:evaluatesHypothesis <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/hypothesis/morphoeval-lobo-limbform-morphology-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-limbform-audit-lobo-limbform-morphology-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/2026-10-14-limbform-audit-lobo-limbform-morphology-10>,
